    "question": {
      ":question/id": "6e4fcf8a-bb36-5a86-85bb-e9f1d6551b32",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $X$ into the matrix $W$, where\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nW=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 9\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that the $2$nd and the $1$st rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $3$rd row. \n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $3$rd row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+4\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 8 & 3 & 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =W.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+4{R}_{2}.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
