      ":question/problem": "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $S$ into the matrix $T$, where\n\n$$\nS=\\begin{bmatrix}15 & 0 & 30 \\\\ 60 & 0 & 120 \\\\ 20 & 0 & 39\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nT=\\begin{bmatrix}15 & 0 & 30 \\\\ 65 & 0 & \\frac{519}{4} \\\\ 20 & 0 & 39\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that the $1$st and $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $2$nd row.\n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $2$nd row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =\\begin{bmatrix}15 & 0 & 30 \\\\ 60 & 0 & 120 \\\\ 20 & 0 & 39\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{3} \\\\ & \\sim\\begin{bmatrix}15 & 0 & 30 \\\\ 65 & 0 & \\frac{519}{4} \\\\ 20 & 0 & 39\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ & =T.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{3}.\n$$",
